expected_issues.description:
`cleanPoints()` assumes `points.length >= 2`. If `extractPoints()` returns an empty/1-point contour/hole (degenerate shapes, or after earlier processing), `points[0]`/`currentPos.x` will throw. Add a guard like `if ( points.length < 2 ) return;`.

```suggestion
				if ( points.length < 2 ) return;
				let prevPos = points[ 0 ];
```

